WEBVTT

00:00.880 --> 00:02.710
<i>The Earth team
made it to the playoffs,</i>

00:03.380 --> 00:05.340
<i>but lost their first two races.</i>

00:05.760 --> 00:07.590
<i>Basically, they were
headed out the door.</i>

00:08.090 --> 00:10.220
<i>So Don Wei
called in the cavalry...</i>

00:10.970 --> 00:12.970
<i>Me, Rick Thunderbolt,</i>

00:13.180 --> 00:16.680
<i>former champion star-racer pilot,
and now...</i>

00:16.850 --> 00:18.480
<i>the new coach
for the Earth team.</i>

00:18.770 --> 00:20.520
<i>Everything went
smoothly after that.</i>

00:21.060 --> 00:22.440
<i>We won the next race.</i>

00:23.020 --> 00:24.610
<i>But Molly's holding
something back.</i>

00:25.320 --> 00:26.570
<i>I can feel it.</i>

00:27.110 --> 00:28.740
<i>I hope she'll open up.</i>

01:38.100 --> 01:40.140
OK, Molly.
Now, give me the edge.

01:40.430 --> 01:41.350
Check.

01:43.230 --> 01:44.560
Triple spin, clockwise!

01:49.280 --> 01:50.690
Good thing I ate light.

01:51.400 --> 01:52.650
Jordan, instead of whining,

01:52.780 --> 01:55.490
why don't you switch the turret
and aim towards the rear?

01:55.820 --> 01:57.370
Sorry, Rick.
I'm on it.

02:01.410 --> 02:03.120
Is that the best
you can do, Molly?

02:03.500 --> 02:05.750
Give me the same,
counterclockwise.

02:06.040 --> 02:07.210
Come on,
keep doing your best!

02:15.590 --> 02:17.050
How was today's training?

02:17.220 --> 02:18.850
-We're doomed.
-What?

02:21.060 --> 02:24.020
They're making good progress.
You'll be very happy.

02:24.810 --> 02:25.650
OK, people.

02:25.810 --> 02:28.150
Let's get it together.
It's almost time!

02:29.690 --> 02:31.990
I'm counting on all of you
to do your very best

02:32.150 --> 02:33.860
and win today's race.

02:34.070 --> 02:35.410
Me, me, me.

02:35.860 --> 02:38.200
A simple "good luck"
would be nice, just once.

02:48.420 --> 02:49.960
Thinking about your dad again?

02:50.420 --> 02:52.760
My dad?
But how did you...

02:52.920 --> 02:55.970
You told me he was your reason
for racing, didn't you?

02:56.130 --> 02:58.220
Yes, I did, of course.

02:58.430 --> 02:59.430
Um, my dad.

02:59.930 --> 03:01.350
Well, now's the time
to show Daddy

03:01.520 --> 03:03.600
what you're really
made of, little mouse.

03:03.770 --> 03:05.350
Refueling complete.

03:07.730 --> 03:09.440
Even if he can't see you
from Earth,

03:09.610 --> 03:12.070
I'm sure your dad
feels your victories.

03:12.570 --> 03:14.360
System's OK.
It's a go.

03:14.740 --> 03:15.700
Thank you, Rick.

03:19.740 --> 03:23.790
But unfortunately, my dad
happens to be a complete jerk!

03:31.210 --> 03:33.630
For the fourth round
of the playoffs,

03:33.960 --> 03:38.260
we now call forth
the Earth team!

03:39.180 --> 03:41.680
And from Planet Byrus,

03:41.850 --> 03:45.730
Rush, aboard the Stone Crusher!

03:54.940 --> 03:56.900
Hey, Jordan.
Take a look at that.

03:57.650 --> 03:59.570
That fat Santa
doesn't scare me.

04:09.420 --> 04:11.880
Well, not really.

04:16.760 --> 04:19.050
That ship looks too heavy to be fast.

04:19.220 --> 04:21.550
-Koji?
-Fused magma for propulsion.

04:21.720 --> 04:23.310
Extremely resistant exterior.

04:23.930 --> 04:25.970
There's no telling
how much thrust he has.

04:26.220 --> 04:27.390
Keep digging-

04:27.560 --> 04:29.520
Remember, I don't like surprises.

04:30.020 --> 04:32.610
Today's playoff will have
a special rule.

04:37.110 --> 04:38.530
Target race.

04:38.860 --> 04:41.660
A target race?
I like the sound of that one.

04:41.990 --> 04:43.910
Stan, do you know
what that means?

04:44.200 --> 04:45.120
I haven't a clue.

04:45.370 --> 04:47.790
They're surprise targets,
no doubt.

04:48.210 --> 04:49.410
Come on, Don. Relax.

04:49.580 --> 04:51.710
Trust the kids to do their thing.

04:51.880 --> 04:53.540
As if I had a choice.

05:05.220 --> 05:06.850
Out of my way!

05:07.350 --> 05:09.020
I need this victory!

05:12.440 --> 05:14.400
Molly!
I can't hold him off!

05:18.820 --> 05:19.650
Not good.

05:19.990 --> 05:21.990
<i>Molly,
remember your training.</i>

05:24.240 --> 05:25.410
It's edge time.

05:30.120 --> 05:31.290
Yeah, that's my girl.

05:31.500 --> 05:32.920
That was so not cool.

05:39.880 --> 05:42.880
Sir, I think you should know
that the alien ship is cruising

05:43.050 --> 05:45.100
at only 30% of its capacity.

05:45.260 --> 05:47.260
In other words,
he's dragging his feet.

05:47.430 --> 05:48.850
Why on earth would he do that?

05:53.020 --> 05:54.810
Ah, there they are.

06:09.660 --> 06:11.040
1 point for Rush.

06:11.200 --> 06:14.460
And an extra bonus point
for being the first to score.

06:15.540 --> 06:18.500
The one who destroys
the most targets in the shortest time

06:18.670 --> 06:19.750
will be today's winner.

06:20.920 --> 06:22.920
Molly, the spheres!
They're your targets!

06:23.470 --> 06:24.590
[Don Wei] Turn back at once!

06:25.930 --> 06:27.180
That's it!

06:28.640 --> 06:29.970
Jordan, hit them!

06:31.180 --> 06:31.810
[gasps]

06:49.740 --> 06:52.910
Almost... there...

06:53.710 --> 06:54.580
Gotcha!

06:56.670 --> 06:58.080
And now for your friend.

07:04.760 --> 07:07.340
Earth team, 1, Rush, 5.

07:07.550 --> 07:08.550
Faster, Molly.

07:08.720 --> 07:10.890
Without this victory,
we're finished.

07:11.060 --> 07:12.180
Find the targets!

07:12.720 --> 07:14.270
Cut her some slack, Don.

07:14.430 --> 07:16.270
You're only going
to freak her out.

07:16.440 --> 07:18.560
Rick, I asked you
to coach them, not me.

07:18.730 --> 07:19.770
All right?

07:23.490 --> 07:25.320
Bye-bye, kiddies.

07:25.610 --> 07:28.160
And on to the Ultimate Prize.

07:40.500 --> 07:43.630
This is the wrong tunnel!
He's got all the targets on his side!

07:44.010 --> 07:45.510
Try the infrared sensors.

07:51.810 --> 07:52.720
Bingo!

07:57.100 --> 07:59.230
Watch out, Jordan.
We're leaving the tunnel.

08:03.980 --> 08:06.190
The Earth team has destroyed
four targets.

08:07.320 --> 08:09.780
Didn't see that one coming,
did you, big guy?

08:10.070 --> 08:11.700
Rush has destroyed five.

08:12.700 --> 08:16.710
The revised score is
5 for the Earth team and 10 for Rush!

08:25.800 --> 08:27.300
Molly, what are you doing?

08:27.420 --> 08:29.260
Don't let him control the race!

08:29.430 --> 08:31.680
What do you think I'm doing?
Knitting you a sweater?

08:36.600 --> 08:38.640
Great, now I'm color-blind.

08:45.360 --> 08:47.820
Molly, do me a favor.
Give me an edge.

08:47.940 --> 08:49.530
Whatever makes you happy.

09:01.500 --> 09:02.750
Hidden targets!

09:09.760 --> 09:13.510
The new score is 24 to 24!

09:24.150 --> 09:25.820
Buckle up, Jordan,
we're back to racing!

09:31.360 --> 09:33.030
Now, you're forcing me
into the wall!

09:45.290 --> 09:46.170
One more.

09:48.840 --> 09:52.300
Jordan, I hope you're OK,
because I got a real treat for you.

09:52.470 --> 09:54.010
I'm all over it.

09:56.510 --> 09:58.140
Come on, Jordan.

09:58.260 --> 09:59.560
Don't blow this.

10:04.810 --> 10:05.940
It's mine!

10:30.670 --> 10:32.220
-Yahoo!
-We won!

10:35.470 --> 10:36.180
Yeah!

10:36.340 --> 10:37.510
That's incredible!

10:38.720 --> 10:40.350
I'm getting too old for this.

10:40.520 --> 10:42.600
Well, you did the best
you could to stop them,

10:42.770 --> 10:43.940
but they still won the race.

10:46.980 --> 10:51.150
Final score,
the Earth team, 25, Rush, 24.

10:51.610 --> 10:53.740
Earth team wins!

11:12.840 --> 11:14.550
Bravo, Jordan!

11:15.340 --> 11:17.390
You saved the day, my boy!

11:17.640 --> 11:19.010
That was excellent shooting.

11:19.180 --> 11:22.220
-It was nothing, sir.
-Now, now, pull yourself together.

11:22.680 --> 11:24.480
We have more races to win.

11:32.980 --> 11:34.320
Molly, I...

11:34.490 --> 11:36.740
I must congratulate you, too.
It was a tough race.

11:37.450 --> 11:39.910
And you fared, er, beautifully.

11:41.740 --> 11:42.700
Thank you, sir.

11:49.920 --> 11:52.880
Hop on, Jordan.
A change of scenery will do us good.

11:53.050 --> 11:54.340
Let's blow this pop stand.

11:57.380 --> 11:58.550
I can't breathe in here.

12:03.640 --> 12:06.770
You've really got a problem
with this girl, don't you, huh?

12:07.850 --> 12:10.770
I'm tough with all my pilots.
You should know that.

12:11.310 --> 12:13.570
Maybe it's time
you got a life, Don.

12:13.980 --> 12:16.780
My life is perfectly fine
as it is, thank you.

12:16.900 --> 12:17.900
Yeah, right.

12:18.070 --> 12:19.740
I'd sure hate to be your son,

12:20.490 --> 12:22.660
or for that matter,
your daughter.

12:28.120 --> 12:29.460
Did I say something wrong?

12:30.710 --> 12:33.460
I'm not sure I'm up
for a long ride, Molly.

12:42.260 --> 12:44.760
Besides, these fields
all look the same to me.

12:45.140 --> 12:48.060
Jordan, you really have
no sense of adventure.

12:48.230 --> 12:49.020
Hang on!

12:59.200 --> 13:00.610
You had a family?

13:00.780 --> 13:02.620
How come you never told me?

13:05.950 --> 13:08.040
You remember when we first met?

13:08.330 --> 13:09.660
Yeah, sure.

13:46.030 --> 13:47.870
Hey! Hey, old man.
You busy?

13:48.040 --> 13:49.700
We need someone
to give us a start.

13:50.710 --> 13:51.750
Excuse me?

13:53.040 --> 13:53.920
We're racing.

13:54.080 --> 13:56.340
Or is that
not obvious enough for you?

13:58.550 --> 14:00.880
You want me to start a race?

14:13.100 --> 14:15.770
Oh, man. You are out there!

14:18.400 --> 14:19.610
OK, fine.

14:19.780 --> 14:21.030
<i>I'll do it, but...</i>

14:21.190 --> 14:23.530
Don't shift so early this time.

14:39.460 --> 14:42.550
<i>You won that race
and every one after it.</i>

14:50.850 --> 14:52.680
Thanks to your great coaching.

14:53.140 --> 14:55.600
From the moment
we worked together,

14:55.770 --> 14:58.110
it was the beginning
of a new life for me.

14:58.520 --> 15:01.570
But I didn't say much
about my previous life.

15:05.280 --> 15:07.700
You see, I've been
a manager before.

15:07.870 --> 15:09.990
A married man
with a young daughter.

15:12.700 --> 15:17.210
The death of my first champion
turned my world upside down.

15:17.630 --> 15:20.500
I lost the desire to carry on.

15:21.710 --> 15:24.760
I cut all links to my past
in order to survive.

15:26.800 --> 15:29.510
I can't believe that you managed
to keep this from me

15:29.970 --> 15:31.890
all these years.

15:39.560 --> 15:41.270
This island is filled with ruins.

15:41.440 --> 15:44.440
But they don't look like anything
the Scrubs would build, do they?

15:44.650 --> 15:45.860
I never thought about it.

16:00.080 --> 16:01.790
I'm going to check this one out.

16:01.960 --> 16:02.590
What?

16:05.970 --> 16:07.430
Hey, Molly?

16:08.180 --> 16:10.600
I think we should head back.
It'll be dark soon.

16:12.970 --> 16:14.270
Oh, come on.

16:14.430 --> 16:16.560
You think Don Wei is going
to worry about us?

16:19.270 --> 16:21.230
Look! There's
an opening up there!

16:21.400 --> 16:22.230
Molly!

16:23.770 --> 16:25.400
Jordan, take a look at this place.

16:25.820 --> 16:27.110
It's totally amazing!

16:27.280 --> 16:30.160
You can clean your guns later.
I'm going in there.

16:30.530 --> 16:32.330
Come on.
Let's get out of here.

16:32.490 --> 16:33.990
This place gives me the creeps.

16:38.370 --> 16:39.290
Molly! Mo...

16:46.840 --> 16:48.800
Molly! Are you OK?

17:11.910 --> 17:13.950
What are these sculptures?

17:14.660 --> 17:17.120
Strange.
They look like star-racers.

17:18.370 --> 17:20.540
But that's impossible.

17:20.790 --> 17:24.420
This temple is ancient.
It must be thousands of years old.

17:39.520 --> 17:41.560
Molly, get out of there!
It's sinking!

17:51.070 --> 17:52.150
Molly!

18:07.130 --> 18:08.420
Head for dry land.

18:08.590 --> 18:10.380
There's nothing
you can do for her now.

18:36.160 --> 18:37.200
Molly...

18:51.420 --> 18:52.420
Molly!

19:02.640 --> 19:03.890
Molly.

19:13.820 --> 19:16.240
Molly, are you all right?

19:17.910 --> 19:19.370
You saved me. But why?

19:20.330 --> 19:22.160
I was following you.

19:22.540 --> 19:25.460
I wanted to congratulate you
on your victory.

19:28.080 --> 19:30.290
It was truly a splendid race!

19:32.920 --> 19:36.090
You mean you're really happy for us?
I don't understand.

19:44.020 --> 19:45.850
I lost the race today.

19:46.020 --> 19:47.650
But I'll surely win tomorrow.

19:47.810 --> 19:51.230
On my planet, we pride ourselves
on seeing the bright side of life.

19:51.820 --> 19:54.690
My ram's horn is always half full.

20:01.410 --> 20:03.910
Come, I'll drive you back
to your pit.

20:04.370 --> 20:07.670
You both had
enough excitement for one day.

20:18.680 --> 20:21.300
Mom, I need a big hug.
